# ==================================================================================================
# WHAT NEVER ENTERS THE BUILD CONTEXT                                            SEC-A2R §3 §6
# ==================================================================================================
# A .dockerignore is not a build-speed optimisation here. Everything listed below, if copied in,
# would be present in an image layer FOREVER - and an image layer is not deleted by a later RUN rm.
# A private key that appears in layer 3 and is removed in layer 4 is still in the image, still in the
# registry, and still pullable by anyone who can pull the tag.
# ==================================================================================================

# Restored by `npm ci` inside the builder stage from the lockfile. Copying the host's tree in would
# ship whatever the developer happened to have, including dev dependencies and platform binaries.
node_modules/

.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# Real configuration. `.env.example` is excluded too: the image must take its settings from the
# environment, and a file full of placeholders sitting next to the code is an invitation to edit it.
.env
.env.*

# TEST KEYS AND TEST TOKENS ARE THE POINT OF THIS FILE. The end-to-end generates RSA key pairs and
# mints JWTs; none of that may be reachable from a production container, where its only possible use
# is by someone who got in.
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
secrets/
test/
tests/
__tests__/
*.test.js
coverage/

# Documentation and runbooks describe how to reach production. They belong in the repository.
README.md
*.md
apps-script-verifier/

npm-debug.log*
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
